  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence or absence of a sure outcome (100% probability outcome) in each lottery. As established, neither lottery has a sure outcome, so the reason would either favor both or be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention or consider certainty or sure outcomes in their reasoning. Instead, they focus on the higher payoff in the winning branch of Lottery A. There is no alignment between the information used by the individual (payoff size upon winning) and the information required by the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome). Furthermore, the justification (preferring a higher gain if winning) does not match the rule of the decision reason (prefer the lottery without a sure outcome). Since the individual’s reasoning does not engage with the concept of sure outcomes at all, it is certain that this decision reason was not used.",
